    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Debug the Gap: Maya's Rainbow Page\r\n\r\nMaya wrote this vision:\r\n\r\n> *\"I want a page for my school's photography club. Make it colorful so it stands out and gets people excited to join. The page should have the club name at the top, a short description of what the club does, and a list of upcoming meeting times.\"*\r\n\r\nAnd here's her reaction to what AI built:\r\n\r\n*\"I asked for a colorful page but it looks like a rainbow exploded! Every single thing is a different color. That's not what I meant at all. I wanted it to feel fun and bright, not chaotic.\"*\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. **Diagnose:** Compare Maya's vision to the page. What did AI *think* \"colorful\" meant? What did Maya actually mean?\r\n2. **Fix it by talking to AI Tutor.** You can restate the vision more precisely (\"colorful means 2-3 bright colors that go together, not a different color for everything\"), or direct specific changes step by step - or both.\r\n3. **Judge each change** against Maya's wish before accepting.\r\n\r\nWhen the page feels fun and bright - not chaotic - click **Continue**.",
