    "offer_browser_tts": "true",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** Diagnosis and repair of an over-interpretation failure - AI took \"colorful\" literally and maximally. The skill: articulate what the vague word actually meant, then say it precisely. Students fix it entirely through conversation; the page's vision is quoted in the instructions so nothing requires opening files.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"In one sentence: what went wrong between Maya's vision and this page?\"\r\n- \"What did you say to AI that Maya didn't?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may fix symptoms one element at a time without naming the root cause - ask them to define what Maya meant by 'colorful' first\r\n- Students may over-correct to a boring page - re-read Maya's wish: fun and bright, not plain\r\n",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
